  "body_markdown": "Skip to content\n\nDental Implants\n\nDental Implant Surgery\n\nAll-on-4 Dental Implants\n\nFixed Teeth vs. Removable\n\nCost & Compare\n\nDental Implant FAQ\n\nAesthetics\n\nCosmetic Dentistry\n\nPorcelain Veneers\n\nDental Crowns & Bridges\n\nSmile Makeover\n\nTeeth Whitening\n\nTreatments\n\nSedation Dentistry\n\nOral Surgery\n\nEmergency Dentistry\n\nConditions We Treat\n\nWhat To Expect\n\nPatient Center\n\nInsurance & Financing\n\nSmile Gallery\n\nWho We Are\n\nWhy Choose Us\n\nMeet Dr. Esam Nahlah\n\nMeet The Team\n\nVideo Library\n\nPatient Stories\n\nFor Doctors\n\nReferral Form\n\nContact Us\n\nBlog\n\nCurrent Patients\n\nTysons Corner: (703) 448-3312\n\nAlexandria: (703) 940-5410\n\nNew Patients\n\nTysons Corner: (571) 619-9442\n\nAlexandria: (571) 410-3430\n\nBook now\n\n\n## Book Now\n\n\n\n## Book Now\n\n\n\n# All-on-4 Dental Implants in McLean, VA\n\n\n\n## Your Path to a Brand-New Smile\n\n\n“My Smile Held Me Back, That’s Behind Me Due To My Dental Implants.” – Melanie\n\nSchedule Now\n\n\n## Patient Story\n\n\n\n## A Stunning Smile Transformation\n\n\nFor patients who are missing some or all of their teeth, All-on-4 dental implants offer a permanent, lasting solution that perfectly replicate the look and feel of your natural teeth. While traditional (single) implants attach one tooth to one implant, All-on-4 implants fully reconstruct a patient’s upper and lower arch, using just four titanium implant posts.\n\nAll-on-4 dental implants are far superior to traditional removable dentures for a variety of reasons. They are less prone to slippage and movement over time, they produce less friction on your gums (meaning decreased risk of pain, inflammation and infection), and they are far more comfortable in terms of routine day-to-day maintenance and functionality. If you’re missing some or all of your teeth, All-on-4 dental implants are the best available way to a brand-new and perfect set of teeth.\n\nDr. Nahlah Discusses What is All-On-4\n\n\n## How All-on-4 Dental Implants Work\n\n\nAll-on-4 implants work in a similar manner to single dental implants, but rather than a single tooth, they replace a full (upper and/or lower) arch of teeth! With over 20 years of experience in implant surgery, Dr. Esam Nahlah possesses the intricate skill and technique necessary to engineer a perfect, natural-looking arch of teeth for any patient who is in need of All-on-4 implants.\n\nImplant surgery involves permanent fixation of titanium posts into the jawbone, and this requires adequate dental health to ensure the most effective results. Wondering if Dr. Nahlah’s All-on-4 implants are a practical option for you and your dental needs? Get in touch with our office today [link to Contact Us] to schedule a detailed consultation and oral examination!\n\n\n#### Four Titanium Implant Posts\n\n\nEntire arch of teeth supported by just 4 implant posts\n\nAll-on-4 can replace both upper and lower arches\n\nTitanium posts permanently fuse with the jawbone\n\nNearly identical look and feel compared to natural teeth\n\nFar more cost effective than single implants\n\n\n#### Far Superior to Dentures\n\n\nMore comfortable and less painful than dentures\n\nAll-on-4 implants look and feel just like natural teeth\n\nLess prone to moving and slipping over time\n\nLower long-term cost due to decreased need for maintenance and repairs\n\nEasier hygiene, less prone to inflammation and gum disease\n\n\n#### Long-Lasting Perfection\n\n\nAll-on-4 implants provide decades of use with proper care\n\nFully recreate your perfect smile with a new set of replacement teeth\n\nOffer a full range of functionality\n\nAll-on-4 implants support jaw and facial bone structure\n\nBrush and floss just like your normal teeth\n\n\n### Step 1: Come in for a Personalized Consultation\n\n\nThe first step of All-on-4 dental implant full mouth restoration is to schedule an appointment to meet with Dr. Nahlah. During your initial consultation, he will conduct a full mouth oral examination (including any necessary imaging scans) in order to determine the state of your current oral health.\n\nIn order for the fixed permanent implants to adequately fuse with the jawbone, a patient needs to have minimal bone loss. During your initial consultation, Dr. Nahlah will perform an extensive 3D scan of your mouth using a Cone-beam CT scanner. This will allow Dr. Nahlah and his team to adequately determine if All-on-4 implants are a practical option for you.\n\nTogether we’ll discuss the best option for you and if you’d like, you can see before and after case studies from real patients including how their treatment truly changed their lives. Dental implant pricing, insurance coverage, and financing options will also be discussed. If dental implants are best for you, our McClean, VA implant dentist completes precise surgical planning to ensure each implant placed is in the exact angle, depth, and location for optimal, lasting success, and ideal aesthetics.\n\n\n### Step 2: Surgical Placement of Your All-on-4 Implants\n\n\nThe second step of All-on-4 implants is Transformation Day, when the four titanium posts into the jawbone. In most instances, surgery is a single visit process wherein you will leave the office with your polymethyl methacrylate (PMMA) provisional prosthesis. In order to make your surgery experience as seamless and pain-free as possible, Dr. Nahlah offers a full range of sedation options, including nitrous, IV and oral.\n\nDr. Nahlah also uses advanced, state-of-the-art surgical computer guide benefits in order to deliver All-on-4 implants with an unparalleled level of precision and accuracy. This results in a look, feel and functionality that is nearly identical to that of your natural teeth.\n\n\n### Step 3: Come in for Your Follow-up Appointments\n\n\nThe fourth and final step of your All-on-4 implant surgery is placement of the final zirconia prosthesis (your new permanent artificial teeth). From the time of initial surgery (when the titanium posts are inserted into the jaw), roughly three to four months of healing are required until the final prosthesis can be placed. After you receive your new teeth, an additional two- to four-month period is usually required in order to achieve complete healing.\n\nDental Group of Tysons offers warranty on All-on-4 with Precare, which mandates general cleanings every six months. We also offer free second opinions, as well as immediate load solutions, which means you will receive a fully functional set of PMMA teeth as your temporary prosthesis on the same day of your implant surgery.\n\n\n### Step 4: Placement of the Final Prosthesis\n\n\nView More Results\n\nAll-on-4 Implants\n\n\n### Find out if you're a\n\n\n\n## candidate for dental implants\n\n\n\n#### Answer the Following Questions To Learn more about our pricing and financing options.\n\n\nA Customized Dental Implant Treatment Plan Specific To You\n\n\n## Craft A Perfect Smile Today\n\n\nAre you ready to start the process of obtaining a brilliant, brand-new set of teeth and a stunning, perfect smile? If so, get in touch with our office today and speak with one of our dental professionals about All-on-4 dental implant surgery. Whether you’re missing some of your teeth, all of your teeth, or want to upgrade on your current removable dentures, All-on-4 implants can change your life with a beautiful set of brand-new replacement teeth that are far more comfortable and durable than traditional dentures.\n\nReceiving a new set of permanent teeth can truly alter your quality of life, and will help reinstate all of the simple joys that come along with being able to eat, speak and smile with a beautiful, natural-looking set of replacement teeth. We also offer a variety of insurance and third-party financing options, meaning All-on-4 dental implants are an accessible, affordable option, no matter your financial situation.\n\n\n## Our Patients tell the story best\n\n\nPlay\n\n[trustindex no-registration=google]\n\n\n## New Teeth. New Smile. New Beginning.\n\n\nCall Dental Group of Tysons in McLean, VA today and speak with one of our dental professionals about All-on-4 implant surgery.\n\nBook Now\n\nFacebook Instagram Youtube Google\n\n\n#### Contact Us\n\n\nAddresses:\n\nTysons Corner\n\n7901 Jones Branch Dr., Suite 220\n\nMcLean, VA 22102\n\nNew Patients: (571) 619-9442\n\nCurrent Patients: (703) 448-3312\n\nAlexandria\n\n2855 Duke St,\n\nAlexandria, VA 22314\n\nNew Patients: (571) 410-3430\n\nCurrent Patients: (703) 940-5410\n\n\n#### Hours\n\n\nMonday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nTuesday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nWednesday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nThursday: 8:00am – 5:00pm\n\nFriday: 8:00am – 2:00pm\n\nSaturday: Closed\n\nSunday: Closed\n\n\n#### Services\n\n\nAll-On-4® Implants\n\nCrowns & Bridges\n\n\n#### About Us\n\n\nMeet the Doctor\n\nAbout Us\n\nBefore & After Photos\n\n2025 Dr. Nahlah. All rights reserved",
